{-
   The lane-count conversions in a body that cannot count its lanes - refused by name (J143).

   `unpackLow`, `unpackHigh` and `packLanes` relate two lane counts, one twice the other, and a
   signature can state that only as a computed count, which const generics leave open. Where the
   count is a variable - the natural form of a variable lane type, here - there is no body in which
   the pattern could ever be written, so the call is refused where it is made. They used to answer
   nothing with no diagnostic. The four pure rearrangements are deferred instead -
   `ConstGenericVec.Rearrange.yana`.
-}

@noinline
fn (a, b) widened(v: Vec(a)) -> Vec(b) = unpackLow(v)

@noinline
fn (a, b) widenedHigh(v: Vec(a)) -> Vec(b) = unpackHigh(v)

@noinline
fn (a, b) narrowed(v: Vec(a), w: Vec(a)) -> Vec(b) = packLanes(v, w)

fn main() -> Int = 0
